---Helper class to display properties in the write data channel module wizard
---@class UNiagaraDataChannelWriteModuleData : UObject
---@field public DataChannel UNiagaraDataChannelAsset @The source asset to read from
---@field public WriteMode ENiagaraDataChanneWriteModuleMode @Should the generated module append to the data channel or write to an existing element?
---@field public bPublishToGame boolean @Whether the data generated by the niagara data interface should be published to the world game data channel. This is required to allow game BP and C++ to read this data. Setting this to true will have a minor performance impact.
---@field public bPublishToCPU boolean @Whether the data generated by the niagara data interface should be published to CPU emitters in other Niagara systems. Setting this to true will have a minor performance impact.
---@field public bPublishToGPU boolean @Whether the data generated by the niagara data interface should be published to GPU emitters in other Niagara systems. Setting this to true will have a minor performance impact.
---@field public AllocationMode ENiagaraDataChannelAllocationMode @How should we allocate the buffer into which we write data.
---@field public AllocationCount integer @How many elements to allocate for writing per frame? Usage depends on AllocationMode.
---@field public bUpdateDestinationDataEveryTick boolean @Whether this DI should request updated destination data from the Data Channel each tick. Depending on the data channel this could be an expensive search so we should avoid doing this every tick if possible.
---@field public bAutoTransformPositionData boolean @If true then position inputs are automatically transformed from simulation space to world space, so the write works correctly for localspace emitters.
local UNiagaraDataChannelWriteModuleData = {}

